        "cycles": 16,
        "opcode": 71,
        "remark": "Hardware interrupt entry point (never called directly -- see doc/UCODE.md \"Extensibility\"). Disables interrupts (re-enable with <tt>ien</tt> once safe -- otherwise the handler's own first fetch would immediately re-trigger irq). Switches to the alt <tt>x</tt>'/<tt>y</tt>' bank before touching either register, so neither this prologue nor the handler that runs after it ever clobbers the interrupted code's real <tt>x</tt>/<tt>y</tt> -- see <tt>reti</tt>, which switches back. Push the return address onto <tt>(sp)</tt>. Post-decrement <tt>sp</tt> by 4 (width muxed in alongside the forced opcode, read via IOL). Jump to the address in the interrupt vector register.",
